      "body": "> Hi, I am surprised that the model loads, since `mujoco.sdf.sdflib` does not exist anymore you can remove the entire `extension` section from your model. Are you trying to do sdf-sdf collision or mesh-sdf. Usually the too many contact points error happens for mesh-sdf.\n\nHi, quagla,\nThank you for your prompt reply.\nYes, exactly, I am using SDF-SDF collision in my simulation. I run my c++ program, it shows error: too many contact points.\n\nCan I ask if this sdf plugin is supported well for pin-hole simulation? Shall I use the alternative solution (convex decomposition for hole shapes)?\n\nMany thanks!\n",
